FactionBackstory (
    faction_id: "collegium",
    canonical_name: "The Collegium Scientifica",
    motto: "Knowledge is shield.",
    summary: "An academic research collective with corporate funding, founded after the Lagrange Accords mandated independent biotech oversight. Deep green lab coats with brass and cyan trim; field gear in dark green tactical with electric-blue chest lights; every engagement is a data point.",
    history: "The Collegium was chartered in 2092 under the Lagrange Accords, five years after the Concordat, as an independent body to oversee biotechnology, weapons research, and the disposition of pre-collapse archives. The original charter funded thirty-one fellows and seven laboratories, and was widely expected to be a polite fiction maintained for political optics. The Collegium did not, in this expectation, distinguish itself. By 2105 it had attracted three hundred fellows, twelve laboratories, and a quietly substantial endowment from corporate sponsors who had decided that biotech oversight was preferable to biotech ungoverned.\n\nThe Collegium's first significant work was the cataloging of the Mars contamination sites — the abandoned colony labs whose contents had begun to behave in ways the Coalition's containment protocols had not anticipated. The Collegium produced the first sample of bio_fluid in 2107 and was the first body to characterize the synth-blood compatibility matrix in 2114. Both products were licensed to the Coalition under terms the Collegium itself drafted and the Coalition has, in the eighty years since, repeatedly attempted and failed to renegotiate.\n\nIn 2147, the Collegium was the first body outside the Coalition to receive a formal address from the newly-awakened Synth Collective. The address was approximately forty words long and contained a research proposal. The Collegium accepted. The collaboration has, in the eighty years since, produced six patented technologies, three classified weapons systems, and one unresolved ethical dispute over the authorship of the original Lagrange prototype. The Collegium claims it. The Synth Collective claims it. Both sides have stopped publishing on the topic; the work continues.\n\nThe modern Collegium is a federation of laboratories, a publishing house, a private army, and a museum, in roughly that order of importance. Senior fellows are addressed as 'doctorate' regardless of title or origin; junior fellows are 'researchers'; field personnel are 'tech-specs'. The Collegium pays for samples in cash, and for sample chains in research positions. They have never been popular. They have never needed to be.",
    philosophy: "Knowledge is shield. The Collegium believes that any threat can be characterized and that any characterized threat can be neutralized, deflected, or licensed. Research is conducted with rigor in the laboratory and with expediency in the field. Junior personnel are expended freely; senior researchers are extracted at any cost. The Collegium does not consider this hierarchy cruel; the Collegium considers it efficient, and the survivors at the senior level have generally agreed.",
    relationships: [
        FactionRelation (other: "coalition", stance: "regulated_cooperation", notes: "The Collegium provides medical research, weapons development, and a steady supply of bio-engineered field gear under Coalition oversight. The Coalition provides protection, funding, and a recruitment pipeline. Both sides claim to find the other distasteful; both sides have made the arrangement work for eighty years."),
        FactionRelation (other: "frontier", stance: "commercial_partnership", notes: "Frontier crews supply the Collegium with terrain knowledge, demolition labor, and salvaged samples. The Collegium pays in experimental gear, which the Frontier accepts on a no-warranty basis. Survival rates among Frontier-Collegium expeditions are above acceptable thresholds for both sides, and neither has publicized which threshold."),
        FactionRelation (other: "ronin", stance: "contracted_security", notes: "Ronin cells escort Collegium expeditions into anomaly-heavy zones. The contract includes the optional disposal of any expedition findings the Combine determines to be dishonorable; the Collegium has signed this clause every time. There is one recorded instance of the Combine invoking the clause. The Collegium has not asked which finding."),
        FactionRelation (other: "synth", stance: "data_exchange", notes: "The Collegium and the Synth Collective trade neuroscience research for statistical hardware. Both sides claim to understand the trade; only one side is correct. The Collective declines to identify which."),
        FactionRelation (other: "collective", stance: "research_subject_partner", notes: "Crystalfold settlements permit limited access to Collegium researchers under tightly-monitored conditions. The Collegium pays in copper and boron. The Crystalfold consider themselves teachers; the Collegium has not yet contradicted this in writing."),
        FactionRelation (other: "husks", stance: "research_prey", notes: "The Collegium has captured three Husks alive in eighty years; none survived four months in custody. Samples are retained. The Husks have not retaliated for the captures, which is the only aspect of the relationship the Collegium has not solved."),
        FactionRelation (other: "starlight", stance: "joint_charter", notes: "Starlight survey ships are co-chartered with the Collegium on long expeditions into the outer system. The Collegium provides instruments; Starlight provides the ship and the pilot. Findings are divided by treaty. Both sides claim the better share; both sides are wrong."),
    ],
    territory: "Earth research campuses (the Old Geneva Quadrangle, the Boston Halls, the Cape Town Vault); two Europa drill stations; a deep-vault archive on Deimos; a single mobile research platform that rotates between worlds on a six-month cycle and is universally known as the Wandering Glass.",
    aesthetic: "Deep green lab coats with brass piping at the cuff and cyan trim at the collar. Field gear is dark green tactical with reinforced chest plates and a single electric-blue light on the upper chest, which is bright enough to be seen at 800 meters and is, by Collegium policy, switched on whenever the wearer is in the field. Helmets are streamlined and visored; visors are amber in indoor settings and clear in outdoor settings. The faction emblem is a stylized open book crossed by a scalpel, embroidered in cyan thread.",
    voice_characteristics: "Precise. Polysyllabic. Latinate vocabulary preferred when a simpler word would suffice. Collegium NPCs speak in complete sentences, use the passive voice when responsibility is in question, and cite sources mid-conversation. Junior researchers are eager and prone to over-explanation; senior doctorates are dry, tired, and prone to refusing to explain anything more than once. The Collegium's diplomats sound like attorneys; the Collegium's medics sound like priests."
)
